                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 1,
                    "preset": "h4"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "KATIE TEAGUE, Visual Storyteller & Threshold Guide"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "blk_0swvf4r4w2",
          "type": "text",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "content": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "I was told by an elder once that I am someone who walks between worlds. It’s taken me decades to more fully grok what he meant. In service of Life’s unfolding story, I have a foot in the forest and a foot in technology, helping translate this time of planetary metamorphosis into image, form, and meaning."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "My background lies at the intersection of depth psychology, systems change, integral studies, and wilderness rites of passage. I love holding council with groups and I love filmmaking, both arise from a devotion to the sacredness of Life. Through documentary and conversation with philosophers, mystics, positive deviants, and edge dwellers, I explore the shift from separation to kinship, from dominance, control and extraction to regeneration and cultural nourishment."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Story is one of humanity’s oldest technologies for remembering, renewing culture, and building worlds. When we tell stories that serve Life, we participate in the ongoing act of creation itself. My work invites audiences into that sacred remembering — to see, feel, and become part of the living world’s re-imagining of itself through us."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "I sit on the board of 2 amazing non-profits: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "the School of Lost Borders",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "link",
                          "attrs": {
                            "href": "https://schooloflostborders.org/",
                            "newTab": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Community Learning Network",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "link",
                          "attrs": {
                            "href": "https://www.communitylearningnetwork.org/",
                            "newTab": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Equipment used:"
                    }
